{"In the destroy action, if EmbeddableHost.where(id: params[:id]).first returns nil, calling host.destroy will raise a NoMethodError on nil, producing a 500 error instead of a 404": 0.8136349320411682, "When matching a URL back to a stored embeddable host, record_for_host only uses uri.host and passes it directly into lower(host) = ?, so entries saved with a non-default port or different casing will never be matched": 0.34571850299835205, "The INSERT statement in the migration interpolates the host value directly into SQL without quoting or escaping, allowing SQL injection or breaking the migration for values containing quotes": 0.9354223012924194, "When creating a new host, categoryId is never set before saving, so after the server assigns a default category_id (uncategorized), the success handler overwrites the correctly hydrated category with undefined, leaving the model without a category and causing the UI to show a blank category": 0.6026004552841187, "The template displays the category using host.category, but the embeddable host JSON only exposes category_id (no category relationship), so for existing records host.category will be undefined and the category badge will not render correctly": 0.5422128438949585, "The update action never persists any changes to the database and just re-renders the existing object, so any edits made to the category/host relationships will be ignored": 0.4842660129070282, "The association is declared with embed: :ids, which will expose only an embeddable_host_ids array on the serialized embedding, but the existing Ember code reads and mutates embedding.embeddable_hosts as a collection of host records": 0.5368621349334717, "The /fruits/:id Pretender route ignores the requested :id parameter and always returns the first fruit, breaking REST semantics and causing store.find('fruit', 2) to return the record with id 1": 0.9024084210395813}